      "description": "Original synthetic aligned intensity fixtures by OpenCVDataflowGUI contributors (MIT). No external/customer images or equipment I/O. Input pixels are aligned by construction; Pixel grid does not perform registration. truth.json records lighting formulas, injected defects and channel coefficients. Compare raw and adjusted residuals on the same valid inspection population. Image remains original; Adjusted preserves source depth/encoding; contours highlight defects. This is empirical appearance compensation, not physical radiometric calibration. Large defects or texture changes can be learned as illumination; choose known-good fit regions and an appropriate local window. EXPECT PASS: exact 16-bit BGR channel gain/offset changes. Gains [.75,1.25,1.5], offsets [512,-100,256]; per-channel adjusted residuals should approach zero.",
